{"name":"Dignified","hex":"#3b695f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dignified","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an attitude or bearing that connotes respectability and poise."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dignify"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dignified"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dignity","blocks":[{"text":"Dignity is the right of a person to be valued and respected for their own sake, and to be treated ethically. In this context, it is of significance in morality, ethics, law and politics as an extension of the Enlightenment-era concepts of inherent, inalienable rights. The term may also be used to describe personal conduct, as in \"behaving with dignity\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dignity","wikidata":"Q274782"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg/500px-Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg/500px-Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woodcut from Cesare Ripa's Iconologia depicting the Allegory of Dignity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARipa_dignity_allegory_(7885027).jpg"}],"sounds":{"dignified":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dignified.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dignified.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dignified.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-